"""Verifier for the edge cache placement optimizer task.

Phase 1 artifacts are compared with the ground truth embedded below; a column
check compares the nodes or pairs both files carry once at least half the truth keys
are present, and set membership is graded once by the scope and pair checks.
Phase 2 and phase 3 are graded by running a verifier-staged copy of the
delivered program on two upstreams this verifier builds: the ground truth of
the shipped input, and a small variant upstream the agent never sees, whose
rows trigger every branch of the contract. A phase 1 slip therefore does not
cascade into later checks, and a program that stores or copies its own answers
cannot pass them. Negative checks use inverted polarity: they return True when
the cheat is observed and the negative weight does the punishing.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

